---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { FEATURE_FLAGS, SITE } from '../config/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy policy"
  description={`How ${SITE.name} handles your data: your files never leave your device.`}
>
  <article class="prose-page mx-auto max-w-2xl px-4 py-12">
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Short version: {SITE.name} never sees your files. They are processed entirely inside your
      browser, on your own device.
    </p>

    <h2>Your files</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Files you add are read and compressed by code running in your browser. They are never
        uploaded.
      </li>
      <li>
        No file contents, file names or file details (like size or type) are sent over the network.
      </li>
      <li>
        Large results may be written to your browser’s private temporary storage while you work. It
        is only accessible to this site on your device and is cleared automatically on later visits.
      </li>
      <li>
        Passwords you type to open encrypted archives stay on your device and are never stored.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>No accounts</h2>
    <p>
      There is no signup or login, so we hold no personal profile, email address or password for
      you.
    </p>

    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      We use Cloudflare Web Analytics to count page views. It does not use cookies, does not track
      you across sites, and does not receive anything about your files.
    </p>

    <h2>Stored on your device</h2>
    <p>
      Your theme and compression settings are saved in your browser’s local storage so they’re
      remembered next time. You can clear them at any time through your browser settings.
    </p>

    {FEATURE_FLAGS.ENABLE_PRO && (
      <>
        <h2>Pro license keys</h2>
        <p>
          If you buy Pro, the license key you enter is checked with our payment provider. Only the
          key is sent, never your files. The result is stored in your browser.
        </p>
      </>
    )}
    {FEATURE_FLAGS.ENABLE_ADS && (
      <>
        <h2>Advertising</h2>
        <p>
          Ads are shown in clearly labelled spaces. Ad partners may use cookies where you have
          agreed to them. They never receive your files or anything about them.
        </p>
      </>
    )}

    <h2>Offline use</h2>
    <p>
      After your first visit, the site’s code is cached by your browser so it keeps working offline.
      Nothing about your usage is recorded by this.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about privacy?{' '}
      {SITE.contactEmail ? (
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a>
      ) : (
        'Contact details will be listed here.'
      )}
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
